{
 "slug": "test/comparison",
 "about": "Comparing saved measurements: the entries a comparison holds, their labels and range, the mode, detection standing down, the per-tap overlay giving way, each entry's Air/Top/Back taken from its source, and saving and loading a comparison. Each case starts a fresh analyzer (threshold −40, Taps 1) with an empty library and runs its 'steps': the shared steps of tooling/analyzer-steps (settings, setTaps, newTap, guitarTap, advance), and {\"compare\": [files]} (a comparison of those 'files' entries, as a multi-select in the list makes); {\"load\": file} (loaded as a file); {\"multiTap\": bool} (the Taps toggle: the per-tap overlay of the measurement on screen, on or off); {\"saveComparison\": name, \"view\"?: [minFreq, maxFreq, minDB, maxDB]} (saves the comparison shown, with the chart's range 'view'); {\"loadSaved\": true} (loads the last saved record); {\"check\": {...}}. Fields: 'entries' (count), 'labels', 'mode' (live / comparison), 'loadedRange' ([minFreq, maxFreq, minDB, maxDB] — the range the load gives the chart), 'detecting', 'multiTap' (the per-tap overlay is showing), 'tapEntries' (count), 'savedComparison' (the comparison is of saved measurements), 'modeIds' (the first entry's stored map, mode display name → peak, by 'peakNames'), 'entryPeaks' (the first entry's peaks, by name, any order), 'entryGuitarType' (the first entry's guitar type), 'chartPeaks' / 'chartLabels' (whether the analyzer gives the chart the measurement's peaks to mark / to label — none while a comparison is shown), 'modeLines' (whether the chart draws the guitar mode lines — not for a comparison of saved measurements), 'savedRange' (the last saved record's range, [minFreq, maxFreq, minDB, maxDB]), 'savedRecord' (the last saved record — {name, entries} — or null for none added), 'phase' (Swift's raw value), 'complete'. Expected values are Swift's.",
